  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the Home Page**\n\nOkay, I\'m working on the `Home.tsx` component. The primary task is to remove that distracting dustbin image. I\'ve located the section with the image source and am ready to delete it. I am focused on making sure the component looks clean and polished.\n\n\n**Updating the Hero Section**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focused on the hero section. I\'ve updated the text to \"AI Powered Wastage Classification\". Next, I\'m double-checking the existing background image at `https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1542601906990-b4d3fb778b09...` to see if it fits the new text. I\'m also preparing to add the colorful small images for waste categories in the body sections. I am also investigating whether to modify the existing component, or re-write it from scratch.\n\n\n**Optimizing the Hero Section**\n\nI\'ve replaced the existing text with a dynamic headline for the hero section, updating the copy to make it more impactful. I\'ve switched from a smaller, less prominent heading to a much larger, bold, and dynamic headline. I have also deleted the dustbin image and its related elements. I am now focused on fine-tuning the visual impact.\n\n\n**Enhancing Content Display**\n\nI\'m now focused on the content display. I\'ve analyzed the current text and decided to replace the simple icons next to each waste type with actual images, likely sourced from Unsplash, to enhance visual clarity and user engagement. I aim for a more visually intuitive representation of each waste category.\n\n\n**Sourcing New Waste Images**\n\nI\'ve gathered several Unsplash image URLs to replace the simple icons for waste types, aiming for visual clarity. I have found relevant images for cardboard boxes, glass bottles, crushed cans, and paper, and I\'ve also identified a more suitable image of plastic bottles to replace the current one. I\'ve also sourced an image for \"Trash\" to replace the existing icon.\n\n\n**Implementing Image URLs**\n\nI\'ve updated the `LOCAL_CATEGORIES` array to include an `image` field for each waste type, linking relevant Unsplash image URLs to each category. This will significantly improve the visual presentation of each waste type. I\'m now testing these updated images in the component.\n\n\n\n**Integrating Image Enhancements**\n\nI\'ve integrated the updated `LOCAL_CATEGORIES` array with image URLs into the rendering process, focusing on visual appeal. I\'ve also implemented the image display using `object-cover` and `group-hover:scale-105` to create an attractive interactive effect. I am now refining the overall layout to ensure the enhanced images are properly displayed.\n\n\n**Refining Waste Category Labels**\n\nI\'m now refining the waste category labels to enhance clarity and visual appeal. I\'ve updated the display of recyclability status, moving the icon above the waste type title and description. I\'m focusing on the visual hierarchy to make key information easily discernible. I am also planning to improve the contrast, and readability of the status labels.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
