    thinking: "**Reviewing the Project Details**\n\nI am now closely examining the request details. I will ensure that PNG images are used to replace Unsplash photos. I am also planning to vary the colors of the category cards, and to implement waste icons matching the waste categories.\n\n\n**Implementing Style Changes**\n\nI\'m now concentrating on style updates. I\'ll modify the title, making \"AI Powered Wastage Classification\" a different colored font. I\'m updating `LOCAL_CATEGORIES` with new PNG image links, specific icons, and precise Tailwind color classes for the category cards. For example, Cardboard will feature the `Package` icon and amber/yellow color scheme, alongside a cardboard transparent PNG.\n\n\n**Identifying Appropriate Icons**\n\nI\'m now deep-diving into the icon selection, focusing on `lucide-react`. I\'m comparing icons like `Box`, `GlassWater`, `Drum`, `FileText`, `Milk`, and `Trash2` to each waste category. I am selecting `Package` for Cardboard, `GlassWater` for Glass, and considering `Cylinder` for Metal, if it suits well. I\'m also examining possibilities for icons to represent Plastic and Paper.\n\n\n**Defining Color Palette**\n\nI am now establishing a color palette for the category cards, with specific color assignments. I\'ve decided on amber/orange for Cardboard, cyan/teal for Glass, gray/zinc for Metal, blue/indigo for Paper, rose/pink for Plastic, and slate/black for Trash. I\'m exploring reliable sources for transparent PNGs, considering Wikimedia Commons and potential open URLs, since the previous prompt asked for PNG images instead of using Unsplash.\n\n\n**Clarifying Image Guidelines**\n\nI\'m now clarifying image guidelines. Although the original prompt bans emojis on the model page, I\'m now considering 3D icons or illustrations for the homepage, based on the description \"colourful small images of wastage.\" I\'m avoiding emojis due to the system prompt\'s explicit ban, but searching for reliable free image sources. I\'m checking several potential options, including CDN-hosted 3D icons, specific transparent PNGs, and considering image generation as a last resort.\n\n\n**Refining Icon Selection**\n\nI\'m now refining icon selection, and I\'ve rejected the placeholder options as unsuitable. I\'ve switched to utilizing a free icon API, specifically Icons8, and I\'m very satisfied with its reliability. I\'ve curated a list of suitable icons. For example, I\'ve selected \"Open Box\" for Cardboard, \"Wine Glass\" for Glass, \"Tin Can\" for Metal, and I\'m further refining selections for Paper, Plastic, and Trash categories using the API. I am happy with how easily and precisely Icons8 has allowed me to select icons for the project.\n\n\n**Finalizing Icon and Color Selections**\n\nI\'ve completed the icon and color selection for the waste categories. I\'m pleased with the outcome; Icons8 provides PNGs which precisely match the waste category needs. I\'m importing the appropriate icons from `lucide-react` for the final implementation. I\'ve updated the `LOCAL_CATEGORIES` to have a `colorTheme` property. I am finalizing Cardboard with `Package`, Glass with `Wine`, Metal with `Cylinder`, Paper with `Newspaper`, Plastic with `Beaker`, and Trash with `Trash2`, using the chosen color schemes.\n\n\n**Mapping Tailwind Classes**\n\nI\'m now focusing on mapping the `colorTheme` property to Tailwind classes to dynamically update card styles. I\'m creating a `themeMap` object to safely assign Tailwind classes for background, border, text, hover effects, and icon colors based on each `colorTheme`. For example, amber will use a set of classes for the card components. This ensures a consistent and controlled visual style for each category.\n\n\n**Integrating Font Options**\n\nI am now integrating the Google Font options, specifically \"Inter\" for general text and \"Space Grotesk\" for display elements, into the project\'s CSS. I\'m importing the fonts and updating the `src/index.css` file to define them as `--font-sans` and `--font-display` variables, ensuring a visually appealing and readable typography for all components. I\'ll test these fonts now.\n\n\n\n**Verifying Icon Integrity**\n\nI\'m now carefully verifying the icon availability within `lucide-react`, ensuring the consistency of the choices for each waste category. I\'ve confirmed the existence of all icons, including `Package`, `Droplet`, `Database`, `FileText`, `Beaker`, and `Trash2`. I\'ve double-checked that `GlassWater` is the more suitable match for Glass, and am ready to update the configuration accordingly. This confirms the project\'s visual integrity.\n\n\n**Implementing Icon & Theme**\n\nI\'m now implementing the `ICON_MAP` and updating the `themeMap` object with corresponding Tailwind class names. I\'m focusing on ensuring each category has the proper icon and color scheme assigned. For example, I have updated `ICON_MAP` to include the appropriate icons imported from `lucide-react`, like the ArrowRight. Additionally, I\'m setting up the `themeMap` to use the right Tailwind colors.\n\n\n**Refining Tailwind Integration**\n\nI am now focusing on refining the Tailwind integration with the `themeMap`. I\'ve successfully mapped the `colorTheme` properties to their corresponding Tailwind class names. I\'ve updated the card rendering logic to apply these styles dynamically, and the card now displays a dynamic border, shadow, background, text, and hover effects, all dependent on the category. I\'m testing these styles now. I also updated the title and font in the project.\n\n\n**Testing Font Integration**\n\nI am now thoroughly testing the font integration to guarantee both fonts, \"Inter\" and \"Space Grotesk,\" are correctly applied and rendered as expected throughout the project\'s components. I am confirming a clean, effective display of the chosen font styles. I\'m verifying the 3D icons from Icons8 are displayed as transparent PNGs, ensuring a clean visual effect, and verifying the color scheme.\n\n\n**Adjusting Project Name**\n\nI\'m now implementing the project name adjustments across the site. I\'m adding \"AI Powered Wastage Classification\" to both the hero banner and the Navbar. I\'m also ensuring the correct font style and color are used for both elements, maintaining consistency across these key sections. I\'ve successfully modified the `src/components/Navbar.tsx` file to incorporate the new project name in the correct font and color.\n\n\n**Implementing Logo Enhancements**\n\nI\'m now implementing the logo enhancements. I\'ve successfully added a gradient effect to the logo text, ensuring the project name \"Garbage Classification\" is prominently displayed with a visually appealing style. I\'ve also verified the application of the specified font, ensuring the aesthetic is consistent with the desired look and feel across the navbar.\n\n\n\n**Optimizing Data Display**\n\nI\'m now optimizing how data is displayed, specifically for the loading state. I\'m focusing on ensuring a smooth user experience. I will implement a placeholder image that aligns with the color scheme of the category cards. I\'m working to make sure that the placeholder is as good as can be, and will ensure it matches the size of the original images.\n\n\n\n"
